  "posture_summary": "Lee Jae-myung's multi-vector hedging architecture has produced its most concrete institutional outputs to date, with the India-Vietnam swing completing with 15 MOUs anchoring a 2026-2030 India Special Strategic Partnership and 12 inter-governmental agreements plus nuclear energy financing for Vietnam — extending Korean economic statecraft into Southeast Asian nuclear infrastructure. Against this expansion, the week introduces the most significant structural complication of Lee's presidency: the US partial satellite intelligence restriction over the Kusong nuclear site disclosure, which cites multiple accumulated grievances including pending DMZ access legislation, signals that Washington retains operational tools to express displeasure with Lee's inter-Korean engagement and strategic autonomy agenda even within the transactional alliance framework established at Gyeongju. The economic picture bifurcates: BOK Shin now formally inaugurated with CBDC, won internationalization, and cautious/flexible policy priorities confirmed, and Q1 GDP growing 1.7% on AI chip demand, but Samsung faces a May 21 strike threat with talent already draining to SK Hynix in HBM packaging — the most critical semiconductor segment for the AI supercycle. Domestically, Lee's position remains exceptionally strong at 67% approval with PPP at historic lows of 15-20%, though the intelligence controversy gives the PPP its most credible attack vector in months. The Yoon prosecution (30-year request for Pyongyang drone flights) continues processing the old regime legally.",
