      "text": "Shin Hyun-song was inaugurated as BOK governor on April 21. His inaugural address prioritized CBDC and bank-issued deposit tokens over stablecoins — a deliberate digital currency architecture choice that positions the BOK within central bank digital infrastructure debates. He pledged cautious and flexible monetary policy amid Middle East oil shock risks, outlined won internationalization through 24-hour FX trading, and met Finance Minister Koo Yun-cheol to coordinate fiscal-monetary policy. Analysts at Citi and ING raised Q2 rate hike probability based on Q1 1.7% GDP growth. Analysts also warned that semiconductor-led growth conceals structural weakness (Korea Times, April 26). The CoinDesk and multiple crypto-adjacent outlets covered the CBDC angle extensively.",
